# Cloudflare Pages rewrite for the crew/client link routes.
#
# `expo export -p web --output static` emits the dynamic route as a literal
# file named `s/[token].html`, so a real token URL (/s/abc123) is a 404 until
# the host rewrites it. 200 = rewrite (serve that file, keep the URL), not a
# redirect — the client router then reads the real token off location.pathname.
#
# UNVERIFIED against a live Cloudflare Pages deployment: the bracket characters
# in the target path are the part most likely to need percent-encoding (%5B/%5D)
# or a different form. Verify on the first real deploy. If it resists, the
# proven fallback is `"output": "single"` in app.json, which needs no rewrite
# at all — both modes were tested locally and render identically after hydration.
/s/* /s/[token].html 200
